-- title:
--   Residue order equals V-order modulo (π,U)
-- statement:
--   Fix a field $L$ with a valuation subring $A$, a field extension $F$ of $L$, a field $\bar F_1$ over the residue field of $A$, and a regular prolongation $R_1$ of $A$ to $F$ with values in $\bar F_1$: that is, a valuation subring `R₁.integers` of $F$ meeting $L$ exactly in $A$, together with a surjective ring map `R₁.residue` onto $\bar F_1$ whose kernel is the maximal ideal, compatible with the residue map of $A$, and such that every nonzero $f\in F$ has an $L$-multiple lying in `R₁.integers` with nonzero residue. Let $x_1$ be a place of $\bar F_1$ over the residue field of $A$ (a proper valuation subring which is a principal ideal ring and contains the image of the base field), with $\operatorname{ord}$ the associated integer valuation, namely minus the logarithm of its adic valuation. Let $\mathcal N_0\subseteq F$ be a subring, local and Noetherian, all of whose elements lie in `R₁.integers`; let $C\subseteq L$ be a subring contained in $A$ whose image in $F$ lies in $\mathcal N_0$, with a distinguished element $\varpi\in C$, and assume that every $g\in\mathcal N_0$ differs from the image of some element of $C$ by a non-unit. Let $W$ be a complete discrete valuation ring with an irreducible element $\pi$, let $\sigma:W\to\widehat{\mathcal N_0}$ be a ring map into the adic completion of $\mathcal N_0$ at its maximal ideal carrying $\pi$ to the image of $\varpi$, let $E\ge 1$, and let $\iota$ be a ring isomorphism of $\widehat{\mathcal N_0}$ onto the crossing model $\mathrm{MvPowerSeries}(\mathrm{Fin}\,2,W)/(X_0X_1-\pi^E)$ with $\iota\circ\sigma$ equal to the map sending $o\in W$ to the class of the constant $o$; write $U,V$ for the two coordinate classes. Let $x,y\in\mathcal N_0$ be such that $\iota(x)-\gamma U$ lies in the ideal generated by the constant $\pi$ and $V$ for some unit $\gamma$, and $\iota(y)-\gamma' V$ lies in the ideal generated by the constant $\pi$ and $U$ for some unit $\gamma'$. Assume further: for $f\in\mathcal N_0$, the residue `R₁.residue f` vanishes if and only if $\iota(f)$ lies in the ideal generated by the constant $\pi$ and $U$; every non-unit of $\mathcal N_0$ with nonzero residue has $\operatorname{ord}_{x_1}$ of that residue strictly positive; the residue of $x$ vanishes; and the residue of $y$ has $\operatorname{ord}_{x_1}$ equal to $1$. The conclusion is that for every $f\in\mathcal N_0$ and every $n\in\mathbb N$, if the residue of $f$ is nonzero then $\operatorname{ord}_{x_1}$ of that residue is $\ge 0$ (an assertion independent of $n$), and if it equals $n$ then there is a unit $\gamma_f$ of the crossing model with $\iota(f)-\gamma_f V^{n}$ in the ideal generated by the constant $\pi$ and $U$.
--
--   This is the residue law at one end of a node given by a crossing presentation: along the branch cut out by $U$, the order of a function's residue at the place $x_1$ is computed by its $V$-adic leading term modulo $(\pi,U)$. It supplies the order-comparison input for the construction of layer rational node rings from a base rational node ring and a chart, in both its general and its prime-level form.
